1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,160
Abstract Art.
抽象艺术。

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:54,653
Abstract art used to be controversial. On one hand, the artists stopped painting delicate figures but attempted to adopt special techniques to give people different visual impacts. On the other hand, their works, including sculptures carved out of marble or fragile clay, were all with a specific aim of showing feelings.
抽象艺术曾经颇有争议。一方面，艺术家不再描绘精细的人物形象，而是尝试采用特殊技法，给人带来不同的视觉冲击。另一方面，他们的作品，包括用大理石或易碎黏土雕成的雕塑，都有一个明确目的：表达情感。

3
00:00:54,653 --> 00:01:42,247
Some conventional scholars who were allergic to abstract art said it was evidently ridiculous and neither art nor geometry. Their Traditional Art Committee predicted that it would soon disappear. But nowadays, abstract art has become part of the permanent possessions of contemporary civilization.
一些反感抽象艺术的传统学者，说这种艺术显然荒谬可笑，既算不上艺术，也算不上几何学。他们的传统艺术委员会预言，它很快就会消失。然而如今，抽象艺术已经成为当代文明永久财富的一部分。

4
00:01:42,247 --> 00:02:42,707
Galleries along the Madison Avenue give scores of superb exhibitions on typical abstract works, appealing to many who have a preference for abstract art. The Shadow of Egypt, a café in this district, has become the home to those aggressive abstract artists. Consequently, it is not a coincidence for you to meet one of these artists of great reputation in the flesh.
麦迪逊大道沿线的画廊，举办了许多展示典型抽象作品的精彩展览，吸引了许多偏爱抽象艺术的人。“埃及之影”，是这个街区的一家咖啡馆，它成了那些积极进取的抽象艺术家的聚集地。因此，这并非偶然：你可能遇见其中一位声名卓著的艺术家，而且是见到本人。

5
00:02:42,707 --> 00:03:01,600
They are asked for signatures and given bunches of fragrant flowers plus they are given a great deal of praise by their faithful fans.
人们向他们索要签名，送给他们一束束芬芳的鲜花，他们还获得了大量赞美，来自忠实的粉丝。
